'' =============================================================================
''
''   File....... test-vo-s304-pwm-x-zero-fields.spin2
''   Purpose.... VO-S304 on SILICON: in PWM sawtooth %01001 and triangle %01000, what do X[15:0] = 0 (base period)
''               and X[31:16] = 0 (frame count) do -- base period and frame time?
''   Authors.... Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''   E-mail..... stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started.... Oct 2026
''   Updated.... Oct 2026
''
'' =============================================================================

{ WHAT IS DECIDED  (register VO-S304; close-out study step 8; bench-groupD-recheck.md section 4.3)

  No ingested source gives the PWM X zero case.  The PWM pages say only that X.[15..0] "establishes a base period in clock cycles"
  and X.[31..16] "establishes a PWM frame period in terms of base periods" (silicon-doc-text.txt:4038, :4040, :4057, :4059), and that
  "Y.[15..0] is captured, IN is raised, and the process repeats" at the end of a frame (:4044, :4063).  A "zero = 65,536" statement
  exists only for the DAC modes (:3925, "set X.[15..0] to zero (65,536 clocks)", %00001); EF-014 measured that sibling (DAC-noise X=0,
  period 65,534).  Titus prints "0 < n < 65,536" for the NCO modes and X[15:0] = 1 for PWM only (smart-pins-titus-text.txt:511, :551,
  :593-:659).  So for PWM: is a zero field 65,536, 1, or something that never completes a frame?  This program MEASURES it and predicts nothing.

  RIG  (BARE BOARD -- NOTHING ATTACHED, NO PIN IS DRIVEN)
    P4 = M, the PWM smart pin.  TT = %00 (output disabled regardless of DIR, silicon-doc-text.txt:3796), so the pad is never driven.
    The observation is M's own IN: "At the end of a frame ... IN is raised" -- the frame time is the interval between IN rises.
    (The study's 'second smart pin on a jumper' is not needed: recheck section 4.3.)

  DEBUGGER (EF-057)
    DEBUG_COGS = %0000_0001: the debug interrupt lives in cog 0 only.  Every pin operation and every timestamp is taken in a dedicated PASM
    cog started by COGINIT; cog 0 only checks constants, reads the hub mailbox and reports.  Every printed line is built in a hub buffer and
    sent by ONE debug() record.  Compile with pnut-ts -d; nothing on P62.

  CONFIGURATION WORDS, FIELD BY FIELD (WRPIN D = %AAAA_BBBB_FFF_MMMMMMMMMMMMM_TT_SSSSS_0, silicon-doc-text.txt:3731; %SSSSS list :3807-:3841;
  Spin2 symbols spin2-v55-text.txt:1521, :1538-:1539)
    sawtooth  $0000_0012  AAAA=0000 BBBB=0000 FFF=000 M=0 TT=%00 SSSSS=%01001 bit0=0   = P_PWM_SAWTOOTH
    triangle  $0000_0010  AAAA=0000 BBBB=0000 FFF=000 M=0 TT=%00 SSSSS=%01000 bit0=0   = P_PWM_TRIANGLE
    Neither uses the A or B input.  WXPIN word X = X[31:16] (frame count, in base periods) : X[15:0] (base period, in clocks):
      control  $0010_0010  frame 16, base 16        zero base   $0004_0000  frame 4, base 0        zero frame  $0000_0010  frame 0, base 16
    Cog 0 decodes the words at run time, prints the fields and gates on them and on the symbol compositions (control W).

  FRAME TIME (what the documentation implies; the control arm checks it)
    sawtooth: the counter "counts from one up to the frame period" (:4063) -> one frame = FRAME x BASE clocks.
    triangle: "counts from the frame period down to one, then from one back up to the frame period ... the overall update time is TWO frame
    periods times the base period" (:4044-:4046) -> one frame = 2 x FRAME x BASE clocks.
    Control X = $0010_0010: sawtooth 16 x 16 = 256 clocks, triangle 2 x 16 x 16 = 512 clocks.

  ARMS (per mode; each arm preceded by DIRL and WRPIN #0; then WRPIN mode, WXPIN X, DIRH, then WYPIN #1 -- Y after DIRH, the working order,
  EF-011; Y = 1 has no effect on IN)
    C   control      X = $0010_0010      predicted interval 256 (sawtooth) / 512 (triangle); the gate is stability plus a mean within one base
                                         period (16 clocks) of the model, see CONTROLS; else RIG FAIL
    Z1  zero base    X = $0004_0000      H65536: 4 x 65,536 = 262,144 clocks (x2 triangle) ; FAST: frames faster than the loop (the H1 value would be about 4 clocks, x2) ; STUCK: no IN in the window
    Z2  zero frame   X = $0000_0010      H65536: 65,536 x 16 = 1,048,576 clocks (x2) ; FAST: frames faster than the loop (the H1 value would be about 16 clocks, x2) ; STUCK: no IN in the window
    After the six arms the two control arms run again (control after).  Each arm runs REPEATS times; the first IN is discarded (it ends the
    first frame, begun at DIRH), then NINT intervals are timed (20 for C, 5 for Z1 and Z2).  A wait for an IN is bounded by a window of
    3 x the H65536 interval + 4,000 clocks.  On a timeout the engine reads the pin's IN (TESTP) into the record: IN LOW at the timeout =
    no IN (STUCK, or ONE when one IN came first); IN HIGH at the timeout = FAST (frames come faster than the acknowledge loop).

  HOW THE INTERVAL IS TIMED
    SETSE1 selects "INA bit of pin 4 rises" (%001_PPPPPP, silicon-doc-text.txt:2255) -- the pin's IN flag; the event flag is cleared by
    POLLSE1 WC (:2241).  The cog polls it and reads CT at the detection (the detection delay is under one loop of about 16 clocks), then
    acknowledges the pin with AKPIN so that IN can rise again.  The mean over N intervals has an error of under 16 / N clocks (under 1 clock
    for the 20-frame control).  Frames shorter than the acknowledge loop cannot be resolved: IN can be re-raised before the AKPIN, so no
    rising edge follows and the wait times out with IN HIGH, or the measured interval is the loop's floor (about 44-46 clocks per
    poll-acknowledge cycle -- a count of this engine's instructions made in the review, not a documented figure).  An interval of at most
    FAST_LIMIT = 128 clocks (well above that floor; the next real class, H65536 of the zero-base arm, starts near 262,144) is therefore
    reported as FAST = "FASTER THAN THE LOOP (<= 128 clocks)" -- this says nothing about whether the zero field acts as 1; the printed H1
    prediction is for context only.  The IN level at a timeout is read with TESTP (silicon-doc-text.txt:1984, "read pin D bit in INx";
    the same poll-IN idiom at :3851).

  CONTROLS (gating -- a failure prints RIG FAIL and NO VERDICT)
    W : the configuration and X words decode to the fields above and equal their Spin2 symbol compositions.
    C : both control arms, before AND after the Z arms, in every repeat: the first IN arrives, all 20 intervals are timed, the arm is STABLE
        (max - min of the intervals at most CTL_SPAN_MAX = 24 clocks, and the repeat's mean equal to repeat 1's within CTL_REP_TOL = 2 clocks;
        the "after" arms also against the "before" arm of the same mode) and the mean is within +-one base period (CTL_MODEL_TOL = 16 clocks)
        of the frame-time model.  The measured offset (mean - model) of every repeat is PRINTED.  (Proves the IN-interval method; the frame
        model is checked only to one base period because the engine's detection delay is not an exact constant.)
    T : the measuring cog reports done within RIG_TIMEOUT_SEC = 10 s (clkfreq x 10 = 2.0e9 stays below 2^31 = 2.147e9; 20 would wrap negative).

  PRE-REGISTERED OUTCOMES (nothing is predicted; printed by the program before the run)
    Per (mode, zero field) every repeat of the arm falls in one class:
      H65536 : every interval within max(40, 1 %) clocks of the H65536 value  -> the zero field acts as 65,536
      FAST   : every interval at most 128 clocks, or IN high at the timeout     -> frames FASTER THAN THE LOOP (<= 128 clocks); no "= 1" claim
      STUCK  : no IN within the window and IN LOW at the timeout               -> no frame completes
      ONE    : one IN, then none within the window and IN LOW at the timeout
      OTHER  : anything else (the raw intervals are printed)
    DETERMINISTIC = all repeats in the same class.  VERDICT lines: ZERO = 65,536 | FASTER THAN THE LOOP (<= 128 clocks) | STUCK | ONE-SHOT |
    OTHER | INCONCLUSIVE (the repeats disagree).  FAST with fewer intervals timed than asked (NDONE < NINT) says so in the verdict.
    S-304 stays 'kept served until the bench decides'.

  DEVIATIONS FROM THE BRIEF (bench-groupD-recheck.md section 4.3)
    1. The brief says 'AKPIN between' the intervals and '+-2 clocks' for every match.  A cog polling a flag cannot time a single interval to 2
       clocks, so the control gate is stability + a mean within one base period (with the offset printed) and the long H65536 intervals use max(40, 1 %).
    2. The 'H1' hypothesis (4 or 16 clocks, x2 for the triangle) cannot be told from any faster-than-the-loop frame, so it is reported as FAST.
    3. The control arms are run twice (before and after the Z arms) and in every repeat.

  VERIFIED OPCODES AND DATA (pnut-ts -d -l v1.55.8 build 9/19/2026, read from the .lst; object offsets, cog addresses in brackets)
    Symbol table (listing): CFG_SAW = SYM_SAW = $0000_0012, CFG_TRI = SYM_TRI = $0000_0010, X_CONTROL = $0010_0010, X_ZERO_BASE =
      $0004_0000, X_ZERO_FRAME = $0000_0010, SE1_EVENT = $44 (%001_000100), MB_LONGS = $AB (3 + 8 x 3 x 7).
    DEBUG: 2 records, 24 bytes of DEBUG data.  Hub image: armTbl $070 (8 rows x 8 longs), engine $170.  Row 0 = $12, $0010_0010, $14 (20),
      $12A0 (4768 = 3 x 256 + 4,000), $100 (256), $100, 0, 0.  Row 1 = $12, $0004_0000, 5, $000C_0FA0 (790,432 = 3 x 262,144 + 4,000),
      $0004_0000 (262,144), 4, 1, 0.  Row 2 = $12, $0000_0010, 5, $0030_0FA0, $0010_0000 (1,048,576), $10, 2, 0.
    Cog labels: reset_m [$019] one_repeat [$01E] wait_ev [$055] put [$062]; registers a_cfg_..a_win_ [$06D..$070] (setq #3 block read),
      min_ [$07B], inhi_ [$07E], self_id_ [$080].
    Instructions read back from the hub image (the .bin, engine base = armTbl + $100):
      dirl #4 $FD640840   wrpin #0,#4 $FC0C0004   outl #4 $FD640848   waitx #100 $FD64C81F   dirh #4 $FD640841   ret $FD64002D
      setse1 #68 $FD648820   getct tdir_ $FD60E21A   wypin #1,#4 $FC2C0204   pollse1 wc $FD700824
      NEW in the timeout path of wait_ev: testp #4 wc $FD740840   wrc inhi_ $FD60FC6C   cmp inhi_,#0 wc $F214FC00   (then ret $FD64002D)
      (TESTP D/# WC is encoded 001000000 in the S field, silicon-doc-text.txt:5353; WRC D at :5410)

  HOW TO RUN
    1. USB serial connected (DEBUG on P62/P63).  Compile: pnut-ts -d test-vo-s304-pwm-x-zero-fields.spin2
    2. Load to RAM with DEBUG enabled (pnut-term-ts, or PNut Ctrl-F10).
    3. SAVE THE WHOLE CONSOLE OUTPUT -- it is the only record.
    4. Expected run time: the engine under 1 s, the report about 90 lines.  Done when the "VERDICT VO-S304 ..." lines appear, then
       "=== END ===" and DEBUG_END_SESSION.  No END / DEBUG_END_SESSION line within 15 s = a hang or a lost session: power-cycle the board and
       send the LAST line you saw.
    5. Clock: _clkfreq = 200_000_000 assumes the board's 20 MHz crystal; the listing's CLKMODE is $010009FB.  On another crystal every clock
       count here is off by the ratio.
    6. Pins: ONLY P4 is used (TT = %00, never driven, its own IN is read).  NOTHING may be attached to P4.  No other pin is touched.
}

CON ' ---- Rig Parameters ----
  _clkfreq          = 200_000_000
  DEBUG_COGS        = %0000_0001        ' EF-057: debugger in cog 0 ONLY

  PIN_M             = 4                 ' the PWM smart pin (its own IN is the observable)
  SE1_EVENT         = (%001 << 6) | PIN_M    ' SETSE1: INA bit of PIN_M rises (silicon-doc-text.txt:2255)

  REPEATS           = 3                 ' repeats of every arm
  NINT_C            = 20                ' intervals timed in a control arm
  NINT_Z            = 5                 ' intervals timed in a zero arm
  WIN_MARGIN        = 4_000             ' clocks added to 3 x the H65536 interval for the wait window
  FAST_LIMIT        = 128               ' at most this = FAST (the loop floor is ~44-46 clocks; the next real class starts near 262,144)
  CTL_MODEL_TOL     = 16                ' control: mean within +-one base period (BASE_C) of the frame-time model
  CTL_SPAN_MAX      = 24                ' control: max - min of the intervals of one repeat at most this
  CTL_REP_TOL       = 2                 ' control: repeat means (and before/after means) equal within this many clocks
  CLS_ABS_TOL       = 40                ' H65536: tolerance, at least this
  RIG_TIMEOUT_SEC   = 10                ' clkfreq * 10 = 2.0e9 < 2^31; 20 would wrap negative (4.0e9)
  MBOX_DONE         = 1

  ' control X and the zero-field X words
  BASE_C            = 16
  FRAME_C           = 16
  FRAME_Z1          = 4                 ' zero base arm: frame count
  BASE_Z2           = 16                ' zero frame arm: base period
  ZERO_EFF          = 65_536            ' the H65536 hypothesis
  X_CONTROL         = (FRAME_C << 16) | BASE_C
  X_ZERO_BASE       = (FRAME_Z1 << 16) | 0
  X_ZERO_FRAME      = (0 << 16) | BASE_Z2

CON ' ---- Configuration Words ----
  CFG_SAW           = $0000_0012        ' P_PWM_SAWTOOTH
  CFG_TRI           = $0000_0010        ' P_PWM_TRIANGLE
  SYM_SAW           = P_PWM_SAWTOOTH
  SYM_TRI           = P_PWM_TRIANGLE

  ' WRPIN D field positions and widths (silicon-doc-text.txt:3731)
  SHIFT_AAAA        = 28
  MASK_AAAA         = %1111
  SHIFT_BBBB        = 24
  MASK_BBBB         = %1111
  SHIFT_FFF         = 21
  MASK_FFF          = %111
  SHIFT_M           = 8
  MASK_M            = %1_1111_1111_1111
  SHIFT_TT          = 6
  MASK_TT           = %11
  SHIFT_SSSSS       = 1
  MASK_SSSSS        = %1_1111
  MASK_BIT0         = 1
  SSSSS_SAW         = %01001
  SSSSS_TRI         = %01000

CON ' ---- Arms and Mailbox ----
  ' arm rows in run order: three arms per mode, then the controls again
  #0, ARM_SAW_C, ARM_SAW_Z1, ARM_SAW_Z2, ARM_TRI_C, ARM_TRI_Z1, ARM_TRI_Z2, ARM_SAW_C2, ARM_TRI_C2
  ARMS              = 8
  ' arm table longs: the engine reads the first four, cog 0 all
  #0, AC_CFG, AC_X, AC_NINT, AC_WIN, AC_P65, AC_P1, AC_KIND, AC_MODE
  ARM_LONGS         = 8
  ARM_BYTES         = ARM_LONGS * 4
  #0, KIND_C, KIND_Z1, KIND_Z2
  #0, MODE_SAW, MODE_TRI

  ' per arm per repeat: GOT0 (the first IN arrived), NDONE (intervals timed), TOTAL (clocks first IN -> last IN),
  ' MIN and MAX interval, T0 (clocks DIRH -> first IN), INHI (the pin's IN level read at a timeout: 1 = HIGH, 0 = LOW or no timeout)
  #0, R_GOT0, R_NDONE, R_TOTAL, R_MIN, R_MAX, R_T0, R_INHI
  R_LONGS           = 7

  MB_DONE           = 0
  MB_PROG           = 1
  MB_ARMTBL         = 2
  MB_RES            = 3
  MB_LONGS          = MB_RES + ARMS * REPEATS * R_LONGS

  ' classes
  #0, CL_H65536, CL_FAST, CL_STUCK, CL_ONE, CL_OTHER, CL_NONE

CON ' ---- Report Parameters ----
  LINE_MAX          = 400
  DEC_TOP           = 1_000_000_000
  DEC_DIGITS        = 10
  DEC_BASE          = 10
  HEX_DIGITS        = 8
  HEX_BITS          = 4
  HEX_GROUP         = 4
  HEX_LETTERS       = 10

VAR ' ---- Mailbox & Analysis State ----
  long mailbox[MB_LONGS]
  long fail_count
  long armClass[ARMS * REPEATS]
  byte lineBuf[LINE_MAX + 1]
  long linePos


PUB main() | engineCog, startTick
'' Run the S304 rig: check the constants, start the measuring cog, wait for its done flag, report.
''

' Local Variables:
' @local engineCog - cog id COGINIT returned (negative = no free cog)
' @local startTick - CT when the wait for the done flag began

  longfill(@mailbox, 0, MB_LONGS)
  mailbox[MB_ARMTBL] := @armTbl
  fail_count := 0
  linePos := 0
  say(string("=== VO-S304: PWM sawtooth %01001 / triangle %01000 with X[15:0] = 0 and with X[31:16] = 0 ==="))
  ln_s(string("M = P"))
  ln_u(PIN_M)
  ln_s(string(" (TT = %00, never driven; its own IN is timed); "))
  ln_u(REPEATS)
  say(string(" repeats per arm; NOTHING attached"))
  print_predictions()
  say(string(" "))
  say(string("--- CONTROL W: configuration and X words ---"))
  check_rig_constants()
  if fail_count <> 0
    say(string("NO VERDICT: a construction control failed (see RIG FAIL lines above); the measuring cog was not started"))
  else
    engineCog := coginit(COGEXEC_NEW, @engine, @mailbox)
    if engineCog < 0
      say(string("RIG FAIL: no free cog for the measuring engine"))
      say(string("NO VERDICT: nothing was measured"))
    else
      startTick := getct()
      repeat until mailbox[MB_DONE] == MBOX_DONE or (getct() - startTick) > clkfreq * RIG_TIMEOUT_SEC
      if mailbox[MB_DONE] <> MBOX_DONE
        cogstop(engineCog)
        pinclear(PIN_M)
        ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: measuring cog did not report done within "))
        ln_u(RIG_TIMEOUT_SEC)
        ln_s(string(" s; it was in arm index "))
        ln_u(mailbox[MB_PROG])
        say(string("; P4 cleared by cog 0"))
        say(string("NO VERDICT: the measurement did not complete"))
      else
        ln_s(string("measuring cog = "))
        ln_u(engineCog)
        say(string(" (debugger restricted to cog 0)"))
        report()
  finish()


PRI finish()
' Every terminal path ends here. pnut-term-ts ends the run when
' DEBUG_END_SESSION appears in the output (--headless or --exit-on-end-session).
'

  say(string("=== END ==="))
  debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")
  repeat

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' line output.  Text lives in hub (string(...)), not in DEBUG data: each line
' is built in lineBuf and sent by the single debug() record in ln_out().
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI ln_c(ch)
' Append one character to the line (cut at LINE_MAX).
'
' @param ch - the character

  if linePos < LINE_MAX
    lineBuf[linePos++] := ch

PRI ln_s(pStr) | ch
' Append a zero-terminated hub string to the line.
'
' @param pStr - hub address of the string

' Local Variables:
' @local ch - the character being copied

  repeat
    ch := byte[pStr++]
    if ch == 0
      quit
    ln_c(ch)

PRI ln_u(numVal) | divisor, digitVal, bStarted
' Append an unsigned decimal to the line.
'
' @param numVal - the number, read as unsigned

' Local Variables:
' @local divisor - the decimal place being printed
' @local digitVal - the digit at that place
' @local bStarted - a non-zero digit has been printed

  divisor := DEC_TOP
  bStarted := FALSE
  repeat DEC_DIGITS
    digitVal := numVal +/ divisor
    if digitVal <> 0 or bStarted or divisor == 1
      ln_c("0" + digitVal)
      bStarted := TRUE
    numVal := numVal +// divisor
    divisor /= DEC_BASE

PRI ln_h(numVal) | idx, nibble
' Append a long in hex as $XXXX_XXXX.
'
' @param numVal - the number

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - nibble index, 7 (top) .. 0
' @local nibble - the nibble value

  ln_c("$")
  repeat idx from HEX_DIGITS - 1 to 0
    nibble := (numVal >> (idx * HEX_BITS)) & $F
    if nibble < HEX_LETTERS
      ln_c("0" + nibble)
    else
      ln_c("A" + nibble - HEX_LETTERS)
    if idx == HEX_GROUP
      ln_c("_")

PRI ln_bin(numVal, digits) | idx
' Append "%" and the low digits bits of a number.
'
' @param numVal - the number
' @param digits - how many bits

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - bit index

  ln_c("%")
  repeat idx from digits - 1 to 0
    ln_c("0" + ((numVal >> idx) & 1))

PRI ln_out()
' Send the line built so far as one debug() record and start a new line.
'

  lineBuf[linePos] := 0
  debug(zstr_(@lineBuf))
  linePos := 0

PRI say(pStr)
' Append a string and send the line.
'
' @param pStr - hub address of the string

  ln_s(pStr)
  ln_out()

PRI yes_no(bFlag) : pText
' Printable YES / NO.
'
' @param bFlag - TRUE or FALSE
' @returns pText - address of "YES" or "NO"

  if bFlag
    pText := string("YES")
  else
    pText := string("NO")

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' names, pre-registered outcomes and construction controls
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI arm_ptr(armIdx) : pArm
' @param armIdx - 0..ARMS-1
' @returns pArm - hub address of the arm's table entry

  pArm := @armTbl + armIdx * ARM_BYTES

PRI arm_name(armIdx) : pText
' Printable name of an arm.
'
' @param armIdx - 0..ARMS-1
' @returns pText - address of the name

  pText := lookupz(armIdx: string("sawtooth control     "), string("sawtooth X[15:0]=0   "), string("sawtooth X[31:16]=0  "), string("triangle control     "), string("triangle X[15:0]=0   "), string("triangle X[31:16]=0  "), string("sawtooth control (2) "), string("triangle control (2) "))

PRI class_name(clsVal) : pText
' Printable class.
'
' @param clsVal - CL_*
' @returns pText - address of the name

  pText := lookupz(clsVal: string("H65536"), string("FAST"), string("STUCK"), string("ONE"), string("OTHER"), string("(none)"))

PRI print_predictions() | armIdx, pArm
' Print the outcomes fixed before the run, and the arms.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local armIdx - arm being printed
' @local pArm - the arm's table entry

  say(string("PRE-REGISTERED OUTCOMES (fixed before the run; nothing about the zero fields is predicted):"))
  say(string("  frame time = interval between IN rises: sawtooth FRAME x BASE clocks, triangle 2 x FRAME x BASE (silicon-doc-text.txt:4044, :4063)"))
  say(string("  control arm (X=$0010_0010): stable (max-min <= 24, repeats equal within 2) and mean within +-16 (one base period) of 256 / 512, else RIG FAIL / NO VERDICT; the offset is printed"))
  say(string("  zero arm class per repeat : H65536 = every interval within max(40, 1%) of the H65536 value ; FAST = every interval <= 128 clocks or IN HIGH at the timeout"))
  say(string("                              STUCK = no IN in the window and IN LOW ; ONE = one IN then none and IN LOW ; OTHER = anything else (raw intervals printed)"))
  say(string("  VERDICT per (mode, field): ZERO = 65,536 | FASTER THAN THE LOOP (<= 128 clocks) | STUCK | ONE-SHOT | OTHER | INCONCLUSIVE (repeats disagree)"))
  say(string("  arms (X, wait window, H65536 interval, H1 interval for context):"))
  repeat armIdx from 0 to ARMS - 1
    pArm := arm_ptr(armIdx)
    ln_s(string("    "))
    ln_s(arm_name(armIdx))
    ln_s(string(" X="))
    ln_h(long[pArm][AC_X])
    ln_s(string(" intervals "))
    ln_u(long[pArm][AC_NINT])
    ln_s(string(" window "))
    ln_u(long[pArm][AC_WIN])
    ln_s(string(" H65536 "))
    ln_u(long[pArm][AC_P65])
    ln_s(string(" H1 "))
    ln_u(long[pArm][AC_P1])
    ln_out()

PRI check_rig_constants()
' Control W: every configuration word decodes to the published fields and equals its Spin2 symbol composition;
' the X words hold the intended fields.
'

  check_word(string("sawtooth "), CFG_SAW, SYM_SAW, SSSSS_SAW)
  check_word(string("triangle "), CFG_TRI, SYM_TRI, SSSSS_TRI)
  check_x(string("control   "), X_CONTROL, FRAME_C, BASE_C)
  check_x(string("zero base "), X_ZERO_BASE, FRAME_Z1, 0)
  check_x(string("zero frame"), X_ZERO_FRAME, 0, BASE_Z2)
  if SE1_EVENT <> 68
    say(string("RIG FAIL: SE1_EVENT is not %001_000100 (rise of the INA bit of pin 4)"))
    fail_count++

PRI check_x(pLabel, xWord, expFrame, expBase)
' Print one WXPIN word's fields and count a failure if they differ from the intended ones.
'
' @param pLabel - label string
' @param xWord - the word
' @param expFrame - intended X[31:16]
' @param expBase - intended X[15:0]

  ln_s(string("  X "))
  ln_s(pLabel)
  ln_c(" ")
  ln_h(xWord)
  ln_s(string(": X[31:16] (frame) = "))
  ln_u(xWord >> 16)
  ln_s(string("  X[15:0] (base) = "))
  ln_u(xWord & $FFFF)
  ln_out()
  if (xWord >> 16) <> expFrame or (xWord & $FFFF) <> expBase
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: X word "))
    ln_s(pLabel)
    say(string(" does not hold the intended frame / base fields"))
    fail_count++

PRI check_word(pLabel, cfgWord, symWord, expSssss)
' Decode one WRPIN word into its published fields, print them, and count a
' construction failure if any field or the symbol composition disagrees.
'
' @param pLabel - label string for the printed line
' @param cfgWord - the configuration word the measuring cog writes
' @param symWord - the same word composed from the Spin2 v55 symbols
' @param expSssss - expected %SSSSS

  ln_s(string("  "))
  ln_s(pLabel)
  ln_c(" ")
  ln_h(cfgWord)
  ln_s(string(": AAAA="))
  ln_bin((cfgWord >> SHIFT_AAAA) & MASK_AAAA, 4)
  ln_s(string(" BBBB="))
  ln_bin((cfgWord >> SHIFT_BBBB) & MASK_BBBB, 4)
  ln_s(string(" FFF="))
  ln_bin((cfgWord >> SHIFT_FFF) & MASK_FFF, 3)
  ln_s(string(" M="))
  ln_bin((cfgWord >> SHIFT_M) & MASK_M, 13)
  ln_s(string(" TT="))
  ln_bin((cfgWord >> SHIFT_TT) & MASK_TT, 2)
  ln_s(string(" SSSSS="))
  ln_bin((cfgWord >> SHIFT_SSSSS) & MASK_SSSSS, 5)
  ln_s(string(" bit0="))
  ln_u(cfgWord & MASK_BIT0)
  ln_s(string("  symbols="))
  ln_h(symWord)
  ln_out()
  if ((cfgWord >> SHIFT_AAAA) & MASK_AAAA) <> 0 or ((cfgWord >> SHIFT_BBBB) & MASK_BBBB) <> 0 or ((cfgWord >> SHIFT_FFF) & MASK_FFF) <> 0 or ((cfgWord >> SHIFT_M) & MASK_M) <> 0 or ((cfgWord >> SHIFT_TT) & MASK_TT) <> %00 or ((cfgWord >> SHIFT_SSSSS) & MASK_SSSSS) <> expSssss or (cfgWord & MASK_BIT0) <> 0
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: "))
    ln_s(pLabel)
    say(string(" fields differ from the expected AAAA/BBBB/FFF/M = 0, TT = %00, SSSSS, bit0 = 0"))
    fail_count++
  if cfgWord <> symWord
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: "))
    ln_s(pLabel)
    ln_s(string(" word "))
    ln_h(cfgWord)
    ln_s(string(" differs from its Spin2 symbol composition "))
    ln_h(symWord)
    ln_out()
    fail_count++

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' report
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI rec(armIdx, repIdx, fieldIdx) : recVal
' One recorded long.
'
' @param armIdx - arm
' @param repIdx - repeat
' @param fieldIdx - R_*
' @returns recVal - the recorded long

  recVal := mailbox[MB_RES + (armIdx * REPEATS + repIdx) * R_LONGS + fieldIdx]

PRI near(valA, valB, tolVal) : bNear
' @param valA - a value
' @param valB - another
' @param tolVal - tolerance
' @returns bNear - TRUE when they differ by at most tolVal

  bNear := abs(valA - valB) <= tolVal

PRI classify(armIdx, repIdx) : clsVal | pArm, meanVal, p65, tolVal
' Class of one repeat of a zero arm.
'
' @param armIdx - arm
' @param repIdx - repeat
' @returns clsVal - CL_*

' Local Variables:
' @local pArm - the arm's table entry
' @local meanVal - mean interval, clocks
' @local p65 - the H65536 interval
' @local tolVal - tolerance for H65536

  pArm := arm_ptr(armIdx)
  p65 := long[pArm][AC_P65]
  tolVal := (p65 / 100) #> CLS_ABS_TOL
  if rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_GOT0) == 0
    if rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_INHI) == 1
      clsVal := CL_FAST                 ' IN high at the timeout: frames faster than the acknowledge loop
    else
      clsVal := CL_STUCK
  elseif rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_NDONE) == 0
    if rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_INHI) == 1
      clsVal := CL_FAST
    else
      clsVal := CL_ONE
  else
    meanVal := rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_TOTAL) / rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_NDONE)
    if rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_MAX) <= FAST_LIMIT and (rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_NDONE) == long[pArm][AC_NINT] or rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_INHI) == 1)
      clsVal := CL_FAST
    elseif rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_NDONE) == long[pArm][AC_NINT] and near(meanVal, p65, tolVal) and rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_MIN) >= p65 - tolVal and rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_MAX) <= p65 + tolVal
      clsVal := CL_H65536
    else
      clsVal := CL_OTHER

PRI ctl_ref_arm(armIdx) : refArm
' The control arm a control repeat is compared with: the "before" arm of the same mode (itself for the "before" arms).
'
' @param armIdx - control arm
' @returns refArm - the reference arm

  case armIdx
    ARM_SAW_C2:
      refArm := ARM_SAW_C
    ARM_TRI_C2:
      refArm := ARM_TRI_C
    other:
      refArm := armIdx

PRI ctl_mean(armIdx, repIdx) : meanVal
' Mean interval of one repeat (0 when no interval was timed).
'
' @param armIdx - arm
' @param repIdx - repeat
' @returns meanVal - mean interval, whole clocks

  if rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_NDONE) == 0
    meanVal := 0
  else
    meanVal := rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_TOTAL) / rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_NDONE)

PRI control_ok(armIdx, repIdx) : bOk | pArm, pred, refArm
' Whether one repeat of a control arm is stable and near the frame-time model.
'
' @param armIdx - control arm
' @param repIdx - repeat
' @returns bOk - TRUE when the first IN arrived, all intervals were timed, max - min <= CTL_SPAN_MAX, the mean equals repeat 1's
'                (and the "before" arm's) within CTL_REP_TOL and is within CTL_MODEL_TOL of the model

' Local Variables:
' @local pArm - the arm's table entry
' @local pred - the predicted interval
' @local refArm - the arm whose first repeat this one is compared with

  pArm := arm_ptr(armIdx)
  pred := long[pArm][AC_P65]
  refArm := ctl_ref_arm(armIdx)
  bOk := rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_GOT0) == 1 and rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_NDONE) == long[pArm][AC_NINT]
  if bOk
    bOk := rec(refArm, 0, R_GOT0) == 1 and rec(refArm, 0, R_NDONE) == long[pArm][AC_NINT]
  if bOk
    bOk := rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_MAX) - rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_MIN) <= CTL_SPAN_MAX and near(ctl_mean(armIdx, repIdx), ctl_mean(refArm, 0), CTL_REP_TOL) and near(ctl_mean(armIdx, repIdx), pred, CTL_MODEL_TOL)

PRI ln_signed(numVal)
' Append a signed decimal ("+12", "-3", "+0").
'
' @param numVal - the number

  if numVal < 0
    ln_c("-")
    ln_u(-numVal)
  else
    ln_c("+")
    ln_u(numVal)

PRI print_arm(armIdx) | repIdx, meanVal
' Print the records of one arm: per repeat the intervals' count, mean, min, max and time to the first IN.
'
' @param armIdx - arm

' Local Variables:
' @local repIdx - repeat
' @local meanVal - mean interval

  repeat repIdx from 0 to REPEATS - 1
    ln_s(string("  "))
    ln_s(arm_name(armIdx))
    ln_s(string(" repeat "))
    ln_u(repIdx + 1)
    ln_s(string(": first IN "))
    if rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_GOT0) == 1
      ln_u(rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_T0))
      ln_s(string(" clocks after DIRH"))
    else
      ln_s(string("NONE in the window"))
    ln_s(string(" ; intervals timed "))
    ln_u(rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_NDONE))
    if rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_NDONE) > 0
      meanVal := rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_TOTAL) / rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_NDONE)
      ln_s(string(" mean "))
      ln_u(meanVal)
      ln_s(string(" min "))
      ln_u(rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_MIN))
      ln_s(string(" max "))
      ln_u(rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_MAX))
    if rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_GOT0) == 0 or rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_NDONE) < long[arm_ptr(armIdx)][AC_NINT]
      ln_s(string(" ; wait timed out, IN at the timeout = "))
      if rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_INHI) == 1
        ln_s(string("HIGH"))
      else
        ln_s(string("LOW"))
    ln_out()

PRI zero_verdict(zeroArm, pText) | repIdx, clsFirst, bSame, nShort
' The verdict of one zero arm: class per repeat, determinism, one VERDICT line.
'
' @param zeroArm - the zero arm
' @param pText - printable name of the (mode, field)

' Local Variables:
' @local repIdx - repeat
' @local clsFirst - class of repeat 0
' @local bSame - all repeats in the same class
' @local nShort - repeats that timed fewer intervals than asked

  clsFirst := classify(zeroArm, 0)
  bSame := TRUE
  nShort := 0
  repeat repIdx from 0 to REPEATS - 1
    if rec(zeroArm, repIdx, R_NDONE) < long[arm_ptr(zeroArm)][AC_NINT]
      nShort++
  ln_s(string("  "))
  ln_s(pText)
  ln_s(string(": classes by repeat"))
  repeat repIdx from 0 to REPEATS - 1
    ln_c(" ")
    ln_s(class_name(classify(zeroArm, repIdx)))
    if classify(zeroArm, repIdx) <> clsFirst
      bSame := FALSE
  ln_out()
  ln_s(string("VERDICT VO-S304 "))
  ln_s(pText)
  ln_s(string(": "))
  if bSame == FALSE
    ln_s(string("INCONCLUSIVE - the repeats disagree (records above)"))
  else
    case clsFirst
      CL_H65536:
        ln_s(string("ZERO = 65,536 - the field acts as 65,536 (interval within max(40, 1 %) of "))
        ln_u(long[arm_ptr(zeroArm)][AC_P65])
        ln_s(string(" clocks)"))
      CL_FAST:
        ln_s(string("FASTER THAN THE LOOP (<= "))
        ln_u(FAST_LIMIT)
        ln_s(string(" clocks) - frames come faster than the acknowledge loop can resolve (an H1 value would be "))
        ln_u(long[arm_ptr(zeroArm)][AC_P1])
        ln_s(string("; not distinguishable below the loop floor, so no claim about the value of the zero field)"))
        if nShort > 0
          ln_s(string("; in "))
          ln_u(nShort)
          ln_s(string(" of "))
          ln_u(REPEATS)
          ln_s(string(" repeats fewer than "))
          ln_u(long[arm_ptr(zeroArm)][AC_NINT])
          ln_s(string(" intervals could be timed (NDONE < NINT: IN was already high when the loop looked)"))
      CL_STUCK:
        ln_s(string("STUCK - no IN within the window and IN LOW at the timeout; no frame completes (or it is longer than the window)"))
      CL_ONE:
        ln_s(string("ONE-SHOT - one IN, then none within the window (IN LOW at the timeout)"))
      other:
        ln_s(string("OTHER - the intervals match none of 65,536 / fast / stuck (records above)"))
  ln_out()

PRI report() | armIdx, repIdx, bControls
' Print the records, gate on the control arms, decide. Single exit.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local armIdx - arm
' @local repIdx - repeat
' @local bControls - every control arm repeat is as predicted

  say(string(" "))
  say(string("--- RECORDS (intervals between IN rises, clocks) ---"))
  repeat armIdx from 0 to ARMS - 1
    print_arm(armIdx)
  say(string(" "))
  say(string("--- GATE C: control arms, before and after the zero arms ---"))
  bControls := TRUE
  repeat armIdx from 0 to ARMS - 1
    if long[arm_ptr(armIdx)][AC_KIND] == KIND_C
      repeat repIdx from 0 to REPEATS - 1
        ln_s(string("  "))
        ln_s(arm_name(armIdx))
        ln_s(string(" repeat "))
        ln_u(repIdx + 1)
        ln_s(string(": model "))
        ln_u(long[arm_ptr(armIdx)][AC_P65])
        ln_s(string(" measured mean "))
        ln_u(ctl_mean(armIdx, repIdx))
        ln_s(string(" offset "))
        ln_signed(ctl_mean(armIdx, repIdx) - long[arm_ptr(armIdx)][AC_P65])
        ln_s(string(" span (max-min) "))
        ln_u(rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_MAX) - rec(armIdx, repIdx, R_MIN))
        ln_out()
        if control_ok(armIdx, repIdx) == FALSE
          bControls := FALSE
          ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: "))
          ln_s(arm_name(armIdx))
          ln_s(string(" repeat "))
          ln_u(repIdx + 1)
          ln_s(string(" is not stable / not within one base period of the model ("))
          ln_u(long[arm_ptr(armIdx)][AC_P65])
          say(string(" clocks per frame; span <= 24, repeat means equal within 2, mean within +-16)"))
          fail_count++
  ln_s(string("  every control repeat stable and within one base period of the model: "))
  ln_s(yes_no(bControls))
  ln_out()
  say(string(" "))
  if fail_count <> 0
    say(string("NO VERDICT: a gating control failed (see RIG FAIL lines above); the records are printed for diagnosis only"))
  else
    zero_verdict(ARM_SAW_Z1, string("sawtooth X[15:0] = 0 (base period zero)"))
    zero_verdict(ARM_SAW_Z2, string("sawtooth X[31:16] = 0 (frame count zero)"))
    zero_verdict(ARM_TRI_Z1, string("triangle X[15:0] = 0 (base period zero)"))
    zero_verdict(ARM_TRI_Z2, string("triangle X[31:16] = 0 (frame count zero)"))

DAT ' ---- Arm Table (read by cog 0 and by the engine) ----
        ' engine fields: cfg, x, intervals to time, wait window (clocks)
        ' cog 0 fields : H65536 interval, H1 interval, kind, mode
        ' control: frame time = m x FRAME_C x BASE_C ; zero base: m x 65,536 x FRAME_Z1 (H1: m x 1 x FRAME_Z1) ;
        ' zero frame: m x BASE_Z2 x 65,536 (H1: m x BASE_Z2 x 1) ; m = 1 sawtooth, 2 triangle
armTbl  long    CFG_SAW, X_CONTROL,    NINT_C, 3 * 1 * FRAME_C * BASE_C + WIN_MARGIN,   1 * FRAME_C * BASE_C,      1 * FRAME_C * BASE_C,  KIND_C,  MODE_SAW
        long    CFG_SAW, X_ZERO_BASE,  NINT_Z, 3 * 1 * ZERO_EFF * FRAME_Z1 + WIN_MARGIN, 1 * ZERO_EFF * FRAME_Z1,  1 * 1 * FRAME_Z1,      KIND_Z1, MODE_SAW
        long    CFG_SAW, X_ZERO_FRAME, NINT_Z, 3 * 1 * BASE_Z2 * ZERO_EFF + WIN_MARGIN, 1 * BASE_Z2 * ZERO_EFF,    1 * BASE_Z2 * 1,       KIND_Z2, MODE_SAW
        long    CFG_TRI, X_CONTROL,    NINT_C, 3 * 2 * FRAME_C * BASE_C + WIN_MARGIN,   2 * FRAME_C * BASE_C,      2 * FRAME_C * BASE_C,  KIND_C,  MODE_TRI
        long    CFG_TRI, X_ZERO_BASE,  NINT_Z, 3 * 2 * ZERO_EFF * FRAME_Z1 + WIN_MARGIN, 2 * ZERO_EFF * FRAME_Z1,  2 * 1 * FRAME_Z1,      KIND_Z1, MODE_TRI
        long    CFG_TRI, X_ZERO_FRAME, NINT_Z, 3 * 2 * BASE_Z2 * ZERO_EFF + WIN_MARGIN, 2 * BASE_Z2 * ZERO_EFF,    2 * BASE_Z2 * 1,       KIND_Z2, MODE_TRI
        long    CFG_SAW, X_CONTROL,    NINT_C, 3 * 1 * FRAME_C * BASE_C + WIN_MARGIN,   1 * FRAME_C * BASE_C,      1 * FRAME_C * BASE_C,  KIND_C,  MODE_SAW
        long    CFG_TRI, X_CONTROL,    NINT_C, 3 * 2 * FRAME_C * BASE_C + WIN_MARGIN,   2 * FRAME_C * BASE_C,      2 * FRAME_C * BASE_C,  KIND_C,  MODE_TRI

{ MEASURING ENGINE -- runs in its own cog; the ONLY code that touches the pin.
  No debug() here (DEBUG_COGS excludes this cog anyway). PTRA = @mailbox on entry.
  respt_ walks the mailbox in the order the arms run (arm-major, repeat-major, R_LONGS per repeat).
}
DAT             org     0        ' ---- Measuring Engine ----
engine          mov     mb_, ptra
                mov     ptrb, mb_
                add     ptrb, #MB_ARMTBL * 4
                rdlong  armtbl_, ptrb
                mov     respt_, mb_
                add     respt_, #MB_RES * 4
                mov     progp_, mb_
                add     progp_, #MB_PROG * 4
                mov     armptr_, armtbl_
                mov     arm_, #0

.arm            wrlong  arm_, progp_
                mov     ptrb, armptr_
                setq    #3
                rdlong  a_cfg_, ptrb            ' a_cfg_, a_x_, a_nint_, a_win_
                add     armptr_, #ARM_BYTES
                mov     rep_, #REPEATS
.rep            call    #one_repeat
                djnz    rep_, #.rep
                add     arm_, #1
                cmp     arm_, #ARMS             wz
        if_nz   jmp     #.arm

                call    #reset_m                ' leave P4 safe
                wrlong  #MBOX_DONE, ptra        ' done -- always the last write
                cogid   self_id_
                cogstop self_id_

reset_m         dirl    #PIN_M
                wrpin   #0, #PIN_M
                outl    #PIN_M
                waitx   #100
                ret

' One repeat of the current arm: reset, configure (TT = %00: never driven), SETSE1 on IN rising,
' DIRH, WYPIN #1 (Y after DIRH), time the first IN, then a_nint_ intervals.  Writes R_LONGS longs.
one_repeat      call    #reset_m
                wrpin   a_cfg_, #PIN_M
                wxpin   a_x_, #PIN_M
                setse1  #SE1_EVENT              ' clears the SE1 flag
                dirh    #PIN_M
                getct   tdir_
                wypin   #1, #PIN_M
                mov     got0_, #0
                mov     ndone_, #0
                mov     total_, #0
                mov     min_, big_
                mov     max_, #0
                mov     t0_, #0
                mov     inhi_, #0
                call    #wait_ev                ' the first IN: ends the first frame
        if_nc   jmp     #.fin
                mov     got0_, #1
                mov     t0_, wnow_
                sub     t0_, tdir_
                mov     tfirst_, wnow_
                mov     tprev_, wnow_
                akpin   #PIN_M                  ' IN low; the next frame's end raises it again
.k              call    #wait_ev
        if_nc   jmp     #.fin
                mov     dt_, wnow_
                sub     dt_, tprev_
                mov     tprev_, wnow_
                akpin   #PIN_M
                cmp     dt_, min_               wc
        if_c    mov     min_, dt_
                cmp     max_, dt_               wc
        if_c    mov     max_, dt_
                add     ndone_, #1
                cmp     ndone_, a_nint_         wc
        if_c    jmp     #.k
.fin            cmp     ndone_, #0              wz
        if_nz   mov     total_, tprev_
        if_nz   sub     total_, tfirst_
        if_z    mov     min_, #0
                mov     val_, got0_
                call    #put
                mov     val_, ndone_
                call    #put
                mov     val_, total_
                call    #put
                mov     val_, min_
                call    #put
                mov     val_, max_
                call    #put
                mov     val_, t0_
                call    #put
                mov     val_, inhi_
                call    #put
                call    #reset_m
                ret

' Wait for the SE1 event (IN of M rose) for up to a_win_ clocks: C = 1 and wnow_ = CT at the detection,
' C = 0 on timeout.  POLLSE1 WC returns the event flag in C and clears it.  On a timeout the pin's IN level is read
' (TESTP WC) into inhi_ (1 = HIGH): frames faster than the acknowledge loop leave IN high with no rising edge to see.
wait_ev         getct   w0_
.p              pollse1                         wc
        if_c    jmp     #.hit
                getct   w1_
                sub     w1_, w0_
                cmp     w1_, a_win_             wc
        if_c    jmp     #.p
                testp   #PIN_M                  wc
                wrc     inhi_
                cmp     inhi_, #0               wc      ' C = 0: nothing is below 0
                ret                             ' timeout: C = 0
.hit            getct   wnow_
                ret                             ' C still 1 from POLLSE1 (GETCT without WC)

put             wrlong  val_, respt_
                add     respt_, #4
                ret

big_            long    $7FFF_FFFF

mb_             res     1
armtbl_         res     1
armptr_         res     1
respt_          res     1
progp_          res     1
arm_            res     1
rep_            res     1
a_cfg_          res     1                       ' arm fields, in table order (setq block read)
a_x_            res     1
a_nint_         res     1
a_win_          res     1
tdir_           res     1
tfirst_         res     1
tprev_          res     1
w0_             res     1
w1_             res     1
wnow_           res     1
dt_             res     1
got0_           res     1
ndone_          res     1
total_          res     1
min_            res     1
max_            res     1
t0_             res     1
inhi_           res     1
val_            res     1
self_id_        res     1

